 cover features a color photograph F-BTSC during 1975’s proving flights. The rear cover black and white artwork inserts include an early Concorde concept with four separate jet nozzles, a Hawker Siddeley Type 1000 airborne, and a Dassault Super Caravelle shortly after taking off with its landing gear hanging out. I counted 199 black and white pictures, 97 color photographs, and 35 tables. Many of these pictures and illustrations are published here for the first time. The contents include:\n\n  * Introduction\n  * Acknowledgements\n  * Chapter One: Origins and Studies 1 - Background and Proposals in Britain\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nLondon (https://www.cambridge.org/core/books/london/C9EA64175BDA0731359575BE924C7FF5)\nciteturn65search1 [wordlim: 200] Published: 11.8 years ago; Crawled: 3 months ago; Select Contents [Input] ... Knight\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nconcorde.book (https://www.kcl.ac.uk/sspp/assets/icbh-witness/concorde.pdf)\nciteturn65search13 [wordlim: 200] Published: 23.3 years ago; Other useful sources include *Concorde: the Inside Story* by Geoffrey Knight (London: Weidenfeld & Nicolson, 1976); *The Power Game* by Jock Bruce-Gardyne and Nigel Lawson (London: Macmillan, 1976); *Flying Concorde* by Brian Calvert (London: Fontana, 1981); *Brian Trubshaw,Test Pilot* by Brian Trubshaw with Sally Edmonson (Stroud: Sutton Publishing, 1998); and *The Technical Development of Modern Aviation* by Ronald Miller and David Sawers (London: Routledge & Keegan Paul, 1968).\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nConcorde (https://api.pageplace.de/preview/DT0400.9781472819567_A29574898/preview-9781472819567_A29574898.pdf)\nciteturn65search14 [wordlim: 200] Published: 7 months ago; Contents ... service history\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nGetting About : 